# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Job splitting {#job-splitting}"
msgstr "Paghahati ng job {#job-splitting}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When you have to split one job into several because mixed shot or precision\n"
"values in a single job are no longer supported, consider the following:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag kinakailangan mong hatiin ang isang job sa ilan dahil hindi na sinusuportahan ang mixed shot o precision\n"
"values sa iisang job, isaalang-alang ang mga sumusunod:\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Group the PUBs by their target value — one job per distinct value, not one job per\n"
"PUB.** Splitting is a regrouping, so the total number of PUBs you submit does not change.\n"
"For example, given `[A@0.01, B@0.05, C@0.01]`, submit two jobs: `[A, C]` at `precision=0.01` and `[B]`\n"
"at `precision=0.05`. Submitting `A` and `C` as separate jobs is less efficient, as each job comes with a fixed overhead.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pagsamahin ang mga PUB base sa kanilang target value — isang job bawat natatanging value, hindi isang job bawat\n"
"PUB.** Ang splitting ay isang regrouping, kaya hindi nagbabago ang kabuuang bilang ng mga PUB na isu-submit mo.\n"
"Halimbawa, sa `[A@0.01, B@0.05, C@0.01]`, mag-submit ng dalawang job: `[A, C]` sa `precision=0.01` at `[B]`\n"
"sa `precision=0.05`. Ang pag-submit ng `A` at `C` bilang magkahiwalay na job ay hindi gaanong episyente, dahil bawat job ay may fixed overhead.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Learn once and use the noise models in all split jobs.** It is more efficient to\n"
"run a single `NoiseLearnerV3` job over the union of all layers.\n"
"The result of a noise learner job contains a list of `NoiseLearnerV3Result` objects,\n"
"one for each input instruction, and is in the same order as the input list. You can\n"
"use the output of this noise learner job in all the split (Estimator) jobs, and noise\n"
"models for layers not in the PUBs of a split job are ignored.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Matuto nang isang beses at gamitin ang mga noise model sa lahat ng hinating job.** Mas episyente na\n"
"magpatakbo ng iisang `NoiseLearnerV3` job sa union ng lahat ng layer.\n"
"Ang resulta ng isang noise learner job ay naglalaman ng listahan ng mga `NoiseLearnerV3Result` object,\n"
"isa para sa bawat input instruction, at nasa parehong pagkakasunod-sunod ng input list. Maaari mong\n"
"gamitin ang output ng noise learner job na ito sa lahat ng hinating (Estimator) job, at ang mga noise\n"
"model para sa mga layer na wala sa mga PUB ng isang hinating job ay babalewalain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Submit all the split jobs in a `Batch` first, then collect their results.**\n"
"The `Batch` execution mode provides efficient parallel execution when there are multiple jobs.\n"
"However, `job.result()` is blocking, so calling it inside the submission loop serializes the jobs and negates the benefits of using `Batch`.\n"
"Make sure you use the submit-all-then-collect pattern (shown below).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Isumite muna ang lahat ng hinating job sa isang `Batch`, saka kolektahin ang kanilang mga resulta.**\n"
"Ang `Batch` execution mode ay nagbibigay ng episyenteng parallel execution kapag maraming job.\n"
"Gayunpaman, ang `job.result()` ay blocking, kaya ang pagtawag dito sa loob ng submission loop ay nagse-serialize sa mga job at binabawi ang mga benepisyo ng paggamit ng `Batch`.\n"
"Siguraduhing gamitin mo ang submit-all-then-collect na pattern (ipinapakita sa baba).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the following example, `pub1` and `pub2` require `precision=0.5`, whereas `pub3` requires `precision=0.1`:\n"
msgstr "Sa sumusunod na halimbawa, kinakailangan ng `pub1` at `pub2` ang `precision=0.5`, samantalang kinakailangan ng `pub3` ang `precision=0.1`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
